# Debug statement patterns for stop hook audit
# Format: id@@regex@@message (delimiter: @@)
# Scanned against git diff output when completion is claimed.
# Advisory only — warns but never blocks session exit.
# Lines starting with # are comments. Empty lines are skipped.
#
# Only added lines (starting with +) in the diff are scanned,
# so existing debug statements in untouched code are ignored.

# --- JavaScript/TypeScript ---
console-log@@console\.(log|debug|trace|info)\(@@console.log/debug statement left in code
debugger-js@@\bdebugger\b@@debugger statement left in code

# --- Python ---
print-debug@@\bprint\(.*[Dd]ebug@@print() with debug content left in code
pdb-trace@@\bpdb\.set_trace\b@@pdb debugger left in code
breakpoint-py@@\bbreakpoint\(\)@@Python breakpoint() left in code
ipdb@@\bipdb\.set_trace\b@@ipdb debugger left in code

# --- Ruby ---
binding-pry@@\bbinding\.pry\b@@Ruby binding.pry debugger left in code
byebug@@\bbyebug\b@@Ruby byebug debugger left in code

# --- Rust ---
dbg-macro@@\bdbg!\(@@Rust dbg! macro left in code

# --- Go ---
fmt-println-debug@@fmt\.Println\(.*[Dd]ebug@@Go debug print left in code

# --- General ---
todo-fixme-hack@@\b(TODO|FIXME|HACK|XXX)\b@@TODO/FIXME marker left in code (review before shipping)
